- How would you test with fluctuating CKNE values?
- How would you extend to different log severities and multi-tenant fairness?

## Why This Is Asked

This tests real-time traffic allocation, statistical validity, and multi-tenant fairness under CZNE constraints in a practical feature rollout.

## Key Concepts

- CKNE-weighted exposure and normalization
- Minute-by-minute reallocation under SLA guarantees
- Deterministic seeding for reproducible experiments
- Telemetry, rollback, and drift detection

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: compute per-tenant exposure weights
function computeWeights(tenants){
  const eps = 0.01;
  const sum = tenants.reduce((a,t)=>a+(t.ckne+eps),0);
  return tenants.map(t=>({tenant:t.id, weight:(t.ckne+eps)/sum}));
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle new tenants with no history (cold start)?
- How would you validate statistical significance with overlapping experiments?

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates practical CKNE-aware scheduling at an intermediate level, focusing on rule-based resource quotas and fairness guarantees under load.

## Key Concepts
- CKNE-to-quotas mapping
- Baseline SLA preservation
- Fairness across tenants
- Telemetry and validation

## Code Example
```javascript
function computeLimits(ckne) {
  const concurrency = Math.max(1, Math.floor(5 * ckne));
  const queueDepth = Math.floor(100 * ckne);
  const retryBudget = Math.max(1, Math.floor(3 * (1 - ckne)));
  return {concurrency, queueDepth, retryBudget};
}
```

